# Phase 157: QUESTION Registry (Q → DEC Ledger)

Date: 2026-09-15
Status: DRAFT
Parent DEC: 2026-0915-001 (point #3 — QUESTION→DECISION)

---

## 1. Problem

AI repeats questions across sessions because open questions live
only in conversation memory. DEC-014-style answers exist, but the
question that produced them is not persisted, so the same decision
path gets re-derived or re-asked.

## 2. Solution

A QUESTION entity registry that persists every engineering
question, links it to its resolving DEC, and blocks re-asking
answered questions.

## 3. Entity Schema

```
Q-<nnn>
Question:    <exact question text>
Context:      @context.CTX<id> | <one-line state>
Raised_by:    AI | HUMAN
Raised_at:    <ISO-8601>
Status:       OPEN | ANSWERED | SUPERSEDED
Answer:       DEC-<id>       (when ANSWERED)
Priority:     LOW | HIGH | BLOCKING
```

- BLOCKING question halts the dependent TASK/CASE until answered
  (maps to STOP conditions, /sdd stateful flow).
- SUPERSEDED requires reference to the replacing Q-<id>.

## 4. Flow

```
QUESTION (OPEN)
    ↓ answer recorded
DECISION (DEC-xxx)
    ↓
TASK → CASE → EVIDENCE
```

## 5. Rules

- [Q1] Every non-trivial question asked during D1/S1 MUST be
  registered as Q-<nnn> before a DEC answers it.
- [Q2] A DEC that answers a question MUST reference its Q-<id>.
- [Q3] Re-asking an ANSWERED question is a finding: the AI MUST
  first check the registry (/sdd-decisions surface).
- [Q4] BLOCKING questions MUST surface in /sdd-status.
- [Q5] The registry is append-only; corrections create new entries.

## 6. Location

- `.sdd/projects/<name>/questions/INDEX.sdd` (per-project instance)
- Template: `templates/_sdd/questions/` (scaffolding)

## 7. Integration

- /sdd-decisions: lists OPEN questions alongside decisions
- /sdd-status: surfaces BLOCKING questions
- Decision canvas QUESTION section links @question.Q<id>
